    <td>Invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast, upper outer quadrant at 10 o&apos;clock, presenting as a firm lump after about a year of breast ache; core biopsy: grade 2, estrogen and progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative; clinical stage T2 N0 (cT2 cN0 M0); synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the documented 1811 breast disease and mastectomy, whose cancer diagnosis is debated</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
