<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Seroma under the right mastectomy flap, without infection (L76.34)</content>. A common collection of fluid after drain removal. Afebrile at 36.9 °C with no redness, warmth, or induration, so infection is unlikely and antibiotics are not indicated. The collection is large enough to stretch the flap and is best aspirated by the surgical team, who performed the operation and can judge the flap. [S]<list><item>Telephoned Dr. Marsh&apos;s team, who saw her this afternoon and aspirated 140 mL of clear straw-colored fluid.</item><item>Compression garment day and night for one week; continue gentle shoulder exercises but no lifting over 5 kg.</item><item>Call the breast surgery team the same day for redness, warmth, fever of 38.0 °C or more, cloudy fluid, or rapid reaccumulation.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right breast cancer after total mastectomy (C50.411)</content>. Clear margins and node-negative. The recurrence score from the specimen is pending and will guide adjuvant treatment. [S]<list><item>Primary care review in about ten days with the recurrence score, as planned.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Management of Skin and Soft Tissue Infections: 2014 Update by the Infectious Diseases Society of America (2014)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Breast surgery nurse telephone check in three days. Primary care review in about ten days. Next scheduled visit 1811-10-19: review three weeks after right mastectomy; start of endocrine therapy and survivorship care. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
